menu "KeyRelay"

config YD_OTP_KEYBOARD
    bool "OTP keyboard interface (types the key's OTP on touch)"
    default y
    help
        The receiver shows up as a USB keyboard so that the security key's OTP can be typed when
        you touch it. If you do not use OTPs, turn this off: the receiver then has no keyboard
        interface at all (FIDO + smart card only), which removes the keystroke-injection risk
        described in SECURITY.md. OTP challenge-response through the FIDO interface keeps working.

        OTP（タッチでの入力）を使わないなら n。レシーバーからキーボードの口がなくなり、
        SECURITY.md の「キー入力の差し込み」の危険がなくなる。

choice YD_OTP_KBD_FILTER
    prompt "Keys the OTP keyboard may type"
    depends on YD_OTP_KEYBOARD
    default YD_OTP_KBD_FILTER_MODHEX
    help
        What the receiver is allowed to type when key reports arrive from the desk unit.

        "Yubico OTP only" types nothing but the 16 ModHex letters and Enter, without modifier keys.
        That is all a Yubico OTP (the factory setting of slot 1) contains. Someone who stole the
        pairing key and poses as your desk unit can then not type commands on your computer.

        Choose "Any key" if a slot types a static password, an OATH-HOTP code (digits) or uses the
        Tab options.

        既定の「Yubico OTP only」は、ModHex の16文字と Enter（修飾キーなし）しか打たない。
        Yubico OTP（スロット1の出荷時の設定）はこれだけでできている。ペアリング用の鍵を盗んで
        机上ユニットになりすました相手に、コマンドなどを打ち込まれないようにするため。
        静的パスワード・OATH-HOTP（数字）・Tab の設定を使うスロットがあるなら「Any key」にする。

    config YD_OTP_KBD_FILTER_MODHEX
        bool "Yubico OTP only (ModHex letters and Enter)"

    config YD_OTP_KBD_FILTER_NONE
        bool "Any key (static passwords, OATH-HOTP, Tab)"
endchoice

endmenu
